{"archetypes":[{"name":"rc-chain-integrity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan introduces a 3-layer rc=0/1/2 propagation chain through _verify_failed_jobs_locally → run_ci_fix_vendor → run_evaluate_failure; misrouting rc=2 (head-changed) to rc=1 (bail) silently drops externally-committed fixes, which the plan itself identifies as its most severe failure mode.","prompt_body":"Trace every return-code boundary in the new _verify_failed_jobs_locally → run_ci_fix_vendor → run_evaluate_failure chain. Verify that each propagation hop uses explicit case analysis rather than implicit if-branch collapsing, and that no rc=2 value is accidentally mapped to rc=1 at any boundary. Cross-check the proposed case structure in run_evaluate_failure against the existing _rcc_handle_fix_status contract at scripts/ship-pr.sh:147 and run_per_job_local_fix_loop's rc=2 branch at scripts/ship-pr.sh:2113–2116 to confirm the new vendor path routes head-changed identically. Verify that the plan's refactoring of run_evaluate_failure from `elif run_ci_fix_vendor` to a `case \"$vendor_rc\"` block does not accidentally truncate the existing BAIL_REASON=first-fixer-non-health exit path at approximately line 2135. Check whether adding `local vendor_rc` to run_evaluate_failure's local declarations is sufficient, or whether any early-return or subshell evaluation in the new else-branch could leave vendor_rc unset. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash32-portability","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"BASH_AUTHORING.md §3 mandates bash 3.2 compatibility for all committed shell scripts; the plan's loop replacement and the new helper's array/TSV iteration patterns need explicit verification against the repo's forbidden-constructs list and make lint-bash32.","prompt_body":"Audit every new shell construct the plan introduces against the bash 3.2 forbidden list in BASH_AUTHORING.md §3, specifically: associative arrays (declare -A), namerefs (declare -n/local -n), mapfile/readarray, parameter case conversion (${var^^} etc.), &>> redirection, and coprocs. Examine the proposed C-style arithmetic for-loop replacement (`for ((attempt=1; attempt<=max_iter; attempt++))`) — confirm it is present on the bash 3.2 permitted list or flag it if ambiguous. Check the proposed `case \"$max_iter\" in ''|*[!0-9]*|0)` sanity guard for any extended-pattern or [[ ]] usage that could regress lint-bash32. Examine the new _verify_failed_jobs_locally helper's array usage (unfixable[] append and ${#unfixable[@]} length check) to confirm indexed-array syntax stays within bash 3.2 bounds and would not require a lint-bash32 suppression comment. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
